{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Basic"],"declarations":24,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.massTrace_eq_functional_hol_of_frobeniusForm_eq_counit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.massTrace_eq_functional_hol_of_frobeniusForm_eq_counit","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceIdentity.lean#L201-L207","doc":"With the Frobenius form equal to the counit, the mass is `∫_A(hol w · c)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.massTrace_eq_functional_hol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.massTrace_eq_functional_hol","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceIdentity.lean#L193-L199","doc":"**Mass identity.** The categorical trace of the mass endomorphism of a\ncycle is the functional `x ↦ ∫_A(u · x · c)` evaluated on the cycle's\nmultiplicative integral `x = hol w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.leftTrace_leftMul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.leftTrace_leftMul","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceIdentity.lean#L185-L191","doc":"**Trace of a left multiplication.** `tr(L_y) = ∫_A(y · c)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.frobeniusForm_massIntegrand_of_frobeniusForm_eq_counit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.frobeniusForm_massIntegrand_of_frobeniusForm_eq_counit","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceIdentity.lean#L178-L183","doc":"If the Frobenius form is the counit, `∫_A(Ψ ∘ x) = ∫_A(x)`: the mass of a cycle is the\nFrobenius form of the cycle itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.frobeniusForm_massIntegrand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.frobeniusForm_massIntegrand","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceIdentity.lean#L171-L176","doc":"**The mass integrand applied to a cycle, then integrated.** For `x : 𝟙 ⟶ A`,\n`∫_A(Ψ ∘ x) = ∫_A(u · x)`. This is the well-typed reading of\n`∫_A((∫_A ⊗ id) ∘ Δ ∘ ϱ)`: the composite `𝟙 → A → A → 𝟙` needs no trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.comp_leftMul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.comp_leftMul","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceIdentity.lean#L165-L169","doc":"Left multiplication applied to an element is the convolution product:\n`x ≫ L_y = y * x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.massIntegrand_eq_id_of_frobeniusForm_eq_counit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.massIntegrand_eq_id_of_frobeniusForm_eq_counit","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceIdentity.lean#L160-L163","doc":"If the Frobenius form is the counit, the mass integrand is the identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.density_eq_unit_of_frobeniusForm_eq_counit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.density_eq_unit_of_frobeniusForm_eq_counit","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceIdentity.lean#L155-L158","doc":"If the Frobenius form is the counit, the density is the unit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.massIntegrand_eq_leftMul_density","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.massIntegrand_eq_leftMul_density","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceIdentity.lean#L146-L153","doc":"**The mass integrand is left multiplication by the density.**\n`Ψ = L_u` with `u = Ψ ∘ η`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.leftMul_hol_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.leftMul_hol_cons","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceIdentity.lean#L140-L144","doc":"The endomorphism of a word is the composite of the letters' endomorphisms,\nlast letter acting first. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.hol_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.hol_append","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceIdentity.lean#L133-L138","doc":"The multiplicative integral is multiplicative under concatenation of words. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.conv_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.conv_unit","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceIdentity.lean#L129-L131","doc":"`η` is a right unit for the convolution product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.unit_conv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.unit_conv","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceIdentity.lean#L125-L127","doc":"`η` is a left unit for the convolution product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.conv_assoc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.conv_assoc","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceIdentity.lean#L120-L123","doc":"The convolution product is associative, so `Hom(𝟙, A)` is a monoid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.leftMul_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.leftMul_injective","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceIdentity.lean#L116-L118","doc":"`x ↦ L_x` is injective: `x = η ≫ L_x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.leftMul_conv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.leftMul_conv","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceIdentity.lean#L109-L114","doc":"`L_{x * y} = L_x ∘ L_y`, written in diagrammatic order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.unit_leftMul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.unit_leftMul","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceIdentity.lean#L102-L107","doc":"`L_x ∘ η = x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.leftMul_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.leftMul_unit","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceIdentity.lean#L98-L100","doc":"`L_η = id`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.casimir","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.casimir","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceIdentity.lean#L95-L96","doc":"The Casimir element `c = μ ∘ coev` of the self-duality of `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.density","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.density","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceIdentity.lean#L92-L93","doc":"The density `u = Ψ ∘ η` of the Frobenius form relative to the coalgebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.hol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.hol","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceIdentity.lean#L86-L90","doc":"The discrete multiplicative integral (path-ordered product) of a word of\ntransports, `hol [g₁, …, g_k] = g₁ * (g₂ * ⋯ (g_k * η))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.conv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.conv","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceIdentity.lean#L82-L84","doc":"The convolution product `x * y` on generalised elements `𝟙 ⟶ A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.leftMul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.leftMul","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceIdentity.lean#L78-L80","doc":"Left multiplication `L_x : A → A` by a generalised element `x : 𝟙 ⟶ A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.massIntegrand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceIdentity.massIntegrand","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceIdentity.lean#L73-L76","doc":"The mass integrand `Ψ = (∫_A ⊗ id) ∘ Δ : A → A`, with the left unitor made\nexplicit. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:mass-identity","label":"def:mass-identity","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-identity.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}